</ul><h1>Release The Moisture</h1><p><strong><em>Product Comparison: GENIANI 4-Liter Ultrasonic Cool Mist Humidifier vs.</em> Myst, <em>a game your cousin claims is cool</em></strong></p>
<hr />
<p><strong>GENIANI 4-Liter Ultrasonic Cool Mist Humidifier</strong></p>
<p>PROS:</p>
<ul>
<li>Humidifies spaces up to 376 square feet.</li>
<li>Built-in aromatherapy option allows you to diffuse delightfully fragrant essential oils.</li>
<li>Super quiet operation.</li>
<li>Easy to load.</li>
</ul>
<p>CONS:</p>
<ul>
<li>Only 3 levels of mist.</li>
<li>Not very interactive beyond loading and turning it on.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<p><strong><em>Myst</em>, a game your cousin claims is cool</strong></p>
<p>PROS:</p>
<ul>
<li>Beautiful visuals.</li>
<li>Exciting puzzles.</li>
<li>Allows you to hang out with your cousin, who’s pretty cool.</li>
<li>Many levels (apparently).</li>
</ul>
<p>CONS:</p>
<ul>
<li>Can’t humidify the air.</li>
<li>Doesn’t smell like anything.</li>
<li>On your cousin’s desktop computer, so you only really ever play it at Thanksgiving.</li>
<li>Also ultra quiet, but that’s not a good thing.</li>
<li>Okay, maybe calling the puzzles “exciting” was a bit of an overstatement.</li>
<li>Or, actually, it’s hard to tell, because you’ve never really made it past the first few screens.</li>
<li>When you ask your cousin for help, he says, “I already beat it but I don’t want to give it away,” which you’re pretty sure is a lie to cover up the fact that he hasn’t gotten very far either, despite having continual access.</li>
<li>When you ask if he has any other games, he says, “Yeah, I’ve got <em>Quake</em>,” but then, after you play the first level, he says, “Welp, that’s my favorite level, let’s do something else,” so you’re pretty sure it’s just a demo.</li>
<li>Now you’re starting to wonder if he really beat <em>Echo The Dolphin</em> like he said he did; he claimed he couldn’t show you the later levels because he rented it from the pharmacy and had to return it.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<p>CONCLUSION: We recommend the humidifier if you’re looking for mist, but <em>Myst</em> if you’re looking for <em>Myst</em>.</p>